WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.000
The box model and sizing
An element includes content, padding, border and margin. box-sizing determines which parts are included in its declared width.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Explanation
With content-box, width describes content only; padding and borders are added. With border-box, width already includes content, padding and borders.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Trace the code
.card {
  box-sizing: content-box;
  width: 240px;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 2px solid;
}

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Result
284

240 + 20×2 + 2×2 = 284 px.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Remember
Calculate the example’s outer width, excluding margin. Understand overflow using the box model instead of randomly reducing width.
